git on Luna: why it is here and how it was installed
=====================================================

Installed 2026-10-25 by Mannie (Claude Code), at the user's request, so that
Mannie can work from its own clone of the TANSTAAFLLM repository on Luna.
Record: worklines/mannie/plan_mannie.md, step 6.2, in that repository.

Why not "pacman -S git"
  ArchR's only package repository ([archr], 543 packages) has no git, no perl
  and no tmux. git comes from Arch Linux ARM instead (mirror.archlinuxarm.org,
  aarch64/extra), which is a different distribution.

What was installed (pacman -U, recorded in pacman's database)
  git      2.56.0-1, repacked (see below)
  zlib-ng  2.3.3-1, unchanged (adds only /usr/lib/libz-ng.so*; ArchR's
           libz.so.1 is untouched)
  Both original packages were checked on the desk host: SHA-256 equal to the
  Arch Linux ARM index, and good signatures from "Arch Linux ARM Build System"
  (68B3 537F 39A3 13B3 E574 D067 7719 3F15 2BDB E6A6, as published on
  archlinuxarm.org). ArchR's pacman keyring does not hold that key.

The repack
  The original git package refused to install: it ships a directory
  usr/share/locale, where ArchR has a symbolic link to /storage/.config/locale.
  "--overwrite" would have replaced ArchR's link, so it was not used. Instead
  the package was rebuilt without:
    - usr/share/locale (git's translations; git speaks English)
    - usr/lib/sysusers.d/git.conf (would create a "git" system user)
    - usr/lib/systemd/system/git-daemon* (no git server on Luna)
  Every other file is the signed original. The repack has no signature.
  Its description in "pacman -Qi git" says so.

Dependencies declared but not installed
  pacman was run with --assume-installed for perl, perl-error,
  perl-mailtools and shadow. They are absent from Luna and from ArchR.
  Without perl, a few commands do not work (git send-email, git svn,
  git cvsserver, some "git add -i" paths). clone, commit, push, pull, rebase,
  log and diff work.

Known noise
  Every git command prints, on stderr:
    /usr/lib/libpcre2-8.so.0: no version information available
  git was built against pcre2 10.47 with symbol versions; ArchR's pcre2
  10.45 has none. It is harmless, and git works. ArchR's libpcre2 is also
  used by Sway and glib, so it was not replaced. Some commands also print the
  same notice for libcurl.so.4 (HTTPS only).

To remove
  pacman -R git zlib-ng
  (then remove /usr/bin/git-shell from /etc/shells if pacman leaves it)

If ArchR's repository ever ships git, prefer it: "pacman -R git", then
"pacman -S git".
